<title>USA: Pennzoil sells half its Azeri block interest.</title>
<headline>Pennzoil sells half its Azeri block interest.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennzoil Co said Wednesday it sold about half of its 9.8 percent interest in Azeri-Chirag-Gunashli block in Azerbaijan in exchange for more than $130 million and a fully carried interest on its remaining 4.8 percent share.</p>
<p>Pennzoil also said it will drill seven exploration wells in Azerbaijan, Egypt, Qatar and Australia this year.</p>
<p>In Canada, a joint venture was formed to develop the Zama area of Northern Alberta, while other noncore Canadian assets were sold.</p>
<p>The company began a Gulf of Mexico exploration alliance with Enterprise Oil Plc, which will diversify its exploration risk and allow for accelerated exploring.</p>
</text>
